{"status":"Error","code":"InvalidParameter","error":"The Availability domain is turned off for this company.","nextStep":"Ask an administrator with the Inv. Posting Gate permission set to turn the domain on from the Inventory Setup page. Data.Records.Set cannot change this setup.","hint":"For usage details, call the \"Help.Implementation.Get\" message type with subject \"Inventory.AvailabilityByPeriod.Get\". Always read the help before calling a message type."}

--- Message Type Help ---
{
  "envelope": {
    "subject": {
      "use": "notUsed",
      "forms": [],
      "description": "Subject is not read; the items are named in data.itemNo or data.items."
    },
    "dataRequired": true,
    "version": "1.0",
    "contentType": "text/json"
  },
  "target": [
    {
      "source": "data.itemNo",
      "form": "text",
      "description": "The item whose availability is read. Use items when several items are sent."
    },
    {
      "source": "data.items",
      "form": "array of item nos.",
      "description": "Up to 20 item numbers; use it instead of itemNo, never both."
    }
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "itemNo",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "One item number. Omit it when items is sent."
    },
    {
      "name": "items",
      "type": "array",
      "required": false,
      "description": "Up to 20 item numbers. Do not also send itemNo."
    },
    {
      "name": "variant",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "A variant code of the item. Leave it out to include every variant. A variant that does not exist on the item is refused."
    },
    {
      "name": "location",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "A location code. Leave it out to include every location. A location that does not exist is refused."
    },
    {
      "name": "periodType",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "description": "day, week, month, quarter, or year."
    },
    {
      "name": "from",
      "type": "string",
      "required": true,
      "description": "A date inside the first calendar period, as YYYY-MM-DD."
    },
    {
      "name": "periods",
      "type": "integer",
      "required": true,
      "description": "How many periods to return, from 1 to 53."
    },
    {
      "name": "amountType",
      "type": "string",
      "required": false,
      "description": "netChange (default) reads each period on its own. balanceAtDate reads everything up to the period end."
    }
  ],
  "response": {
    "contentType": "text/json",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "status",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Success."
      },
      {
        "name": "itemNo",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The item number; present when itemNo was sent."
      },
      {
        "name": "description",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The item description; present when itemNo was sent."
      },
      {
        "name": "variant",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The variant code that was sent; empty when none was sent."
      },
      {
        "name": "location",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The location code that was sent; empty when none was sent."
      },
      {
        "name": "periodType",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "day, week, month, quarter or year, in lower case."
      },
      {
        "name": "amountType",
        "type": "string",
        "description": "netChange or balanceAtDate."
      },
      {
        "name": "periods",
        "type": "array",
        "description": "One row per period; present when itemNo was sent.",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "periodStart",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The first date of the period, as YYYY-MM-DD."
          },
          {
            "name": "periodEnd",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The last date of the period, as YYYY-MM-DD."
          },
          {
            "name": "grossRequirement",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The quantity required in the period, for example on sales orders and components."
          },
          {
            "name": "scheduledReceipt",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The quantity scheduled to arrive in the period, for example on purchase orders."
          },
          {
            "name": "plannedOrderReceipt",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The quantity planned to arrive in the period on planned orders."
          },
          {
            "name": "projectedAvailableBalance",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The projected available balance at the end of the period."
          },
          {
            "name": "inventory",
            "type": "decimal",
            "description": "The item ledger quantity within the dates of the period: the net change with netChange, the on-hand quantity at the period end with balanceAtDate."
          },
          {
            "name": "amountType",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "netChange or balanceAtDate."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "items",
        "type": "array",
        "description": "One entry per item, in the order sent; present when items was sent.",
        "children": [
          {
            "name": "itemNo",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The item number."
          },
          {
            "name": "description",
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The item description."
          },
          {
            "name": "periods",
            "type": "array",
            "description": "One row per period.",
            "children": [
              {
                "name": "periodStart",
                "type": "string",
                "description": "The first date of the period, as YYYY-MM-DD."
              },
              {
                "name": "periodEnd",
                "type": "string",
                "description": "The last date of the period, as YYYY-MM-DD."
              },
              {
                "name": "grossRequirement",
                "type": "decimal",
                "description": "The quantity required in the period, for example on sales orders and components."
              },
              {
                "name": "scheduledReceipt",
                "type": "decimal",
                "description": "The quantity scheduled to arrive in the period, for example on purchase orders."
              },
              {
                "name": "plannedOrderReceipt",
                "type": "decimal",
                "description": "The quantity planned to arrive in the period on planned orders."
              },
              {
                "name": "projectedAvailableBalance",
                "type": "decimal",
                "description": "The projected available balance at the end of the period."
              },
              {
                "name": "inventory",
                "type": "decimal",
                "description": "The item ledger quantity within the dates of the period: the net change with netChange, the on-hand quantity at the period end with balanceAtDate."
              },
              {
                "name": "amountType",
                "type": "string",
                "description": "netChange or balanceAtDate."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "errors": [
    {
      "code": "MissingParameter",
      "when": "itemNo is missing and items was not sent, or periodType, from, or periods is missing.",
      "fix": "Send itemNo, or send items with at most 20 item numbers. Also send periodType, from, and periods."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameterFormat",
      "when": "A key has the wrong JSON type.",
      "fix": "Send itemNo as text, from as a date, periods as a whole number, and items as an array of item numbers."
    },
    {
      "code": "UnknownParameter",
      "when": "The request contains a key this type does not read.",
      "fix": "Remove the unknown key. Allowed keys are itemNo, items, variant, location, periodType, from, periods and amountType."
    },
    {
      "code": "RecordNotFound",
      "when": "The item number, variant, or location does not exist.",
      "fix": "Check the item no."
    },
    {
      "code": "ConflictingIdentifiers",
      "when": "itemNo and items were both sent.",
      "fix": "Send either itemNo or items, not both."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "when": "periodType is not day, week, month, quarter, or year, or amountType is not netChange or balanceAtDate.",
      "fix": "Use day, week, month, quarter or year. Use netChange or balanceAtDate for amountType."
    },
    {
      "code": "InvalidParameter",
      "when": "The Availability domain is turned off in Inventory Setup, periods is below 1, or the calendar cannot build every requested period.",
      "fix": "Turn on the Availability domain, or use a periods value from 1 to 53 and a from date inside the calendar."
    },
    {
      "code": "LimitExceeded",
      "when": "periods is above 53, or more than 20 items were sent.",
      "fix": "Split the call."
    },
    {
      "code": "PreconditionFailed",
      "when": "The item is Service or Non-Inventory, so it has no availability.",
      "fix": "Use an inventory item."
    },
    {
      "code": "PermissionDenied",
      "when": "The caller cannot read items, variants, or locations.",
      "fix": "Assign Bifrost Read-Only (extended by Inventory read permissions) and a Business Central permission set that can read these tables."
    }
  ],
  "effect": {
    "effect": "read",
    "writes": false,
    "posts": false,
    "changes": "None. Reads projected availability by calendar period for one or more items.",
    "idempotent": true,
    "permissionSet": "Bifrost Read-Only",
    "preconditions": [
      "The Availability domain is turned on in Inventory Setup.",
      "The caller can read items, item variants and locations."
    ]
  },
  "metering": {
    "chargeable": true,
    "chargedAs": "message"
  },
  "related": [
    {
      "name": "Item.Availability.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Use it for the availability of items per location on one delivery date, instead of per calendar period."
    },
    {
      "name": "Item.Inventory.Get",
      "useInsteadWhen": "Use it for the physical stock on hand per location, without any projection."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Read two months for one item",
      "request": {
        "type": "Inventory.AvailabilityByPeriod.Get",
        "data": {
          "itemNo": "ITEM",
          "periodType": "month",
          "from": "2026-10-16",
          "periods": 2
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": "Success",
        "itemNo": "ITEM",
        "description": "Item",
        "variant": "",
        "location": "",
        "periodType": "month",
        "amountType": "netChange",
        "periods": [
          {
            "periodStart": "2026-10-01",
            "periodEnd": "2026-10-31",
            "grossRequirement": 0,
            "scheduledReceipt": 0,
            "plannedOrderReceipt": 0,
            "projectedAvailableBalance": 0,
            "inventory": 0,
            "amountType": "netChange"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Read one week for items 1000 and 1100 at location BLUE",
      "request": {
        "type": "Inventory.AvailabilityByPeriod.Get",
        "data": {
          "items": [
            "1000",
            "1100"
          ],
          "location": "BLUE",
          "periodType": "week",
          "from": "2026-10-22",
          "periods": 1,
          "amountType": "balanceAtDate"
        }
      },
      "response": {
        "status": "Success",
        "periodType": "week",
        "amountType": "balanceAtDate",
        "variant": "",
        "location": "BLUE",
        "items": [
          {
            "itemNo": "1000",
            "description": "Bicycle",
            "periods": [
              {
                "periodStart": "2026-10-19",
                "periodEnd": "2026-10-25",
                "grossRequirement": 4,
                "scheduledReceipt": 10,
                "plannedOrderReceipt": 0,
                "projectedAvailableBalance": 46,
                "inventory": 40,
                "amountType": "balanceAtDate"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "itemNo": "1100",
            "description": "Front wheel",
            "periods": [
              {
                "periodStart": "2026-10-19",
                "periodEnd": "2026-10-25",
                "grossRequirement": 0,
                "scheduledReceipt": 0,
                "plannedOrderReceipt": 0,
                "projectedAvailableBalance": 25,
                "inventory": 25,
                "amountType": "balanceAtDate"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "overview": "Reads projected availability by calendar period: gross requirement, scheduled receipt, planned order receipt, projected available balance, and inventory. It does not change supply or demand.",
  "notes": "The first period is the calendar period that contains from. With amountType netChange (the default) the amounts cover that period only; with balanceAtDate they cover everything up to the period end. Projected available balance is the balance at the period end in both modes. Inventory is the item ledger quantity within the same dates: the net change of the period with netChange, and the on-hand quantity at the period end with balanceAtDate. One item (itemNo) is answered at the top level; several items (items) are answered in items, each with its own periods. variant and location are exact codes, not filter expressions, and drop shipments are always left out. A service or non-inventory item is refused. At most 53 periods and 20 items are returned. The type only reads, so it can be repeated freely."
}

## Errors and warnings
An error response has `status` = `Error`, a stable `code`, the `error` text and, when they apply, `parameter` (the request parameter concerned, e.g. `lines[2].no`), `received` (the value received), `expected` (what was expected) and `nextStep` (what to do now). `hint` says where to read more.
When a request has several problems, all of them are listed in `errors[]` - each with the same fields - under a top-level `code` (`MultipleErrors`, or a shared code such as `InvalidLine` for the `lines` of a Create type) and a summary `error`. Fix them all before calling again. One problem is reported at the top level, with no `errors[]`.
Request values are checked first and every problem found is reported together. A Business Central validation error raised afterwards, while a record is being written, stops the call and is reported on its own: `code` = `BusinessCentralError`, Business Central's own `error` text, and `parameter` naming the request parameter being applied, e.g. `lines[1].accountNo`. Nothing is written.
Request values are read in one format, whatever the language: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`; date-times ISO 8601 with `Z` or an offset; amounts as JSON numbers (or a string such as `"1234.56"`, no thousands separator); integers as JSON integers; booleans `true` or `false`. Any other value is `InvalidParameterFormat` with `received` and `expected`; for an unambiguous local form such as `26.09.2026`, `nextStep` gives the value to resend. Every bad value of a request is reported together.
Answers are written in one format as well, whatever the language of the call: dates `YYYY-MM-DD`, date-times ISO 8601, numbers with a dot and no thousands separator, and the option and enum values of every answer except `Data.Records.Get` and `Data.Records.Set` as their English names, so a value read from an answer can be sent back. Those two answer the caption of the language of the call, for a person to read. The language of the call (`lcid`) changes captions and message texts, not these forms. Two things are outside Bifrost's control: Business Central writes its own texts (a ledger entry description such as `Direct Cost V00010 on 10/02/26`, the text of a `BusinessCentralError`) with the regional settings of the server session, which `lcid` does not change, so a date in such a text can be in month-day order; and a table view is read with those settings too, so write dates in a view as `YYYY-MM-DD` and decimals with a dot.
Both success and error responses can carry `warnings[]`, each with `code`, `message` and, when they apply, `parameter` and `nextStep`.
`UnknownParameter` refuses undeclared data keys before execution for every type whose effect is not read, including a missing effect. The root envelope option `strict:false` cannot opt out. Read types keep warnings without changing status, validationResult or domain warningCount unless the caller sets `strict:true` (next to type and subject, never inside data). Refusals list the keys and localized nextStep corrections; no business changes or successful execution charges occur. Example: {"type":"Memory.User.Set","strict":true,"data":{"memory":"test","memry":"typo"}} is refused.
`FieldChangedByBC` is a warning from Data.Records.Set: another field validation or the write changed a sent field after its own validation. `parameter` names data[n].fields.{jsonName}, counting from 0. Status stays Success. Compare the returned values with what you sent; follow `nextStep` to use validation order or send the field again in a separate call. Normalisation of the field itself, LCY, Dimension Set ID, BLOB, Media, MediaSet and skipped fields are excluded.
Feature apps (Foundation 28.0.8 or later) can call `Argument.SetErrorContext(Parameter, Expected, NextStep)` before an operation that may fail after writes, then `Argument.ClearErrorContext()` after success. Supply the parameter name and translated labels, never request values, file content, credentials or a call stack. Foundation returns that context on the original `BusinessCentralError` after rollback, including uncaught task errors; `RespondWithLastError()` also uses it. The API does not catch errors, commit data or change the transaction boundary. Keep no-return `Codeunit.Run` and let errors propagate for chained `OmitCommit` calls; never add a Boolean `Codeunit.Run` or a writing `TryFunction` to recover context. Context is cleared between messages. Existing callers without context keep their response shape; recognized lock errors keep their existing `Retryable` guidance.
A message type that must run only one way (Foundation 28.0.9 or later) reads `Argument.GetInvocationSource()`: `Queue` when the task scheduler runs a message the queue API scheduled, `Task` for the Task API (`/tasks`), `Dispatcher` for an internal call through `Dispatcher ori` (the in-product MCP tool server, a nested dispatch from another message type), `Direct` for the Messages page Run Task action and anything unset. Only Foundation sets it; request values, parameters, source, subject and writes to the argument cannot change it. Refuse the other paths with `PreconditionFailed` and a `nextStep` that names the path to use.
`Retryable` means a transient lock or deadlock caught while writing or posting. `error` keeps Business Central's original text. `expected` is "no concurrent lock on the same records"; `nextStep` is "Retry the same call after a few seconds; nothing was changed." Bifrost does not retry automatically. Other platform errors, including uncaught queue-path errors, remain `BusinessCentralError`.
Codes: `MissingParameter`, `InvalidParameterFormat`, `InvalidParameter`, `RecordNotFound`, `AmbiguousRecord`, `ConflictingIdentifiers`, `InvalidFilterField`, `InvalidLine`, `NothingToPreview`, `LinesSkipped`, `BlockedByWriteGuard`, `PreconditionFailed`, `PermissionDenied`, `LimitExceeded`, `BusinessCentralError`, `MultipleErrors`, `DeprecatedParameter`, `UnknownParameter`, `FieldChangedByBC`, `Retryable`, `EULA_REQUIRED`, `TRIAL_NOT_STARTED`. The `error` text may be translated; the code never is.
